\h Ezra
\toc1 Ezra
\toc2 Ezra
\toc3 Ezra
\mt1 Ezra
\is1 Introduction
\ip \bk The account of Ezra\bk*, is like a continuation of \bk The Chronicles\bk*—it tells us about the returning home of other Jews who had been taken to Babylon as captives, and the restoration of daily life in Yerushalem (Jerusalem) and of worshipping at the temple.
\ip It's divided into three main sections: 1. The declaration of King Koresh (Cyrus) of Persia (Heb. Paras) to allow a group of exiled Jews to return to Yerushalem from Babylon. 2. The rebuilding of the temple and its dedication, and the return to worshipping Yahweh there in Yerushalem. 3. The return of a different group of Jewish descendants to Yerushalem under the leadership of Ezra—the one knowledgable about God's instructions. He assisted the Israelis to return to their beliefs and customs, so that their worshipping of the true God wouldn't be forgotten.
\iot Main components of this account
\io1 The first group of exiled Jews return home \ior 1:1–2:70\ior*
\io1 The rebuilding of the temple and its dedication \ior 3:1–6:22\ior*
\io1 Ezra leads other exiles to return to Yehudah (Judah) \ior 7:1–10:44\ior*
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\ie
\c 1
\s1 Koresh returns some Jews
\rem /s1 Return of exiles to Jerusalem; Cyrus Helps the Exiles to Return; End of the Babylonian Captivity; Cyrus Commands the Jews to Return; Cyrus Allows the Exiles to Return
\p
\v 1 In¦217134 the first year¦217134 that Koresh¦217150 \add !(Cyrus¦217150)\add* was king of Persia¦217138 \add (Heb. Paras)\add*, Yahweh¦217142 stirred¦217145 up \add *his\add* spirit¦217149 in¦217162 order¦217139 to fulfil¦217139 what \add *he'd\add* spoken through the prophet Yirmeyah¦217144 \add !(Jeremiah)\add*.\x + \xo 1:1: \xt Jer 25:11; 29:10.\x* \add ≈So¦217134\add* \add @the king\add* distributed an \add official\add* written¦217162 notice¦217156 throughout his kingdom¦217159, saying¦217163,
\v 2 “Koresh¦217167, king¦217168 of Persia¦217169, declares this: Yahweh¦217175, the god¦217176 of heaven¦217177, has¦217173 given¦217173 me all the kingdoms¦217171 in the world, and¦217178 he's appointed¦217180 me to build¦217182 a residence for him¦217184 in Yerushalem¦217186 in Yehudah¦217188.\x + \xo 1:2: \xt Isa 44:28.\x*
\v 3 Anyone among¦217192 you who's¦217212 one of his followers is free to go to Yerushalem (in¦217192 Yehudah¦217202) \add to help\add* build¦217203 a temple there for Yisrael's¦217209 god Yahweh¦217207—the god of Yerushalem. May God¦217197 go with¦217192 you.
\v 4 Those who live near these people¦217227 but¦217215 who are not going themselves, should¦217226 donate gold¦217230 and silver¦217229, and goods¦217231 and livestock¦217232, plus¦217230 cash¦217229 as a voluntary offering¦217235 for¦217236 God's temple in¦217229 Yerushalem¦217239.
\p
\v 5 Then¦217241 \add some\add* of the¦217243 leaders of Benyamin¦217245 and Yehudah¦217244, and \add some\add* priests¦217246 and Levites¦217247—all of whom¦217249 had had their spirits¦217253 stirred¦217249 up¦217254 by God¦217250—left to¦217255 go¦217254 and build¦217255 Yahweh's¦217259 residence in¦217261 Yerushalem¦217261.
\v 6 Their¦217267 neighbours¦217265 had helped them¦217265 by \add ≈donating\add* gold¦217271 and silver¦217270 utensils, goods¦217272 and livestock¦217273, and expensive gifts¦217274, as well as the¦217274 voluntary offerings¦217280 of cash¦217270.
\p
\v 7 Then King¦217283 Koresh¦217284 brought out¦217285 the equipment from Yahweh's¦217291 temple that¦217292 Nevukadnetstsar¦217294 \add !(Nebuchadnezzar¦217294)\add* had brought \add all the way\add* from Yerushalem¦217295 and¦217296 had put¦217296 in¦217297 the house¦217297 of¦217297 his¦217298 gods¦217298.
\v 8 \add *He¦217300\add* \add ≈put the treasurer¦217310 Mitedat in charge of bringing¦217300 them out¦217300\add* and Sheshbatstsar, the ruler of Yehudah¦217314, \add ≈in charge of accepting them and listing them\add*.
\v 9 There were¦217317: thirty¦217320 gold¦217319 basins, one thousand¦217324 silver¦217323 basins, twenty-nine¦217327 knives¦217325,
\v 10 thirty¦217332 gold¦217331 bowls, 410 silver¦217334 bowls, and¦217338 a thousand¦217341 other¦217340 utensils,
\v 11 \add ≈coming to a total¦217344 of 5,400 gold¦217347 and¦217348 silver¦217348 utensils\add*. Sheshbatstsar¦217355 \add ≈took all of that with¦217356 the¦217358 group\add* of exiles¦217358 going from¦217359 Babylon¦217359 to Yerushalem¦217360.
