\c 3
\s1 Rebuilding the altar
\rem /s1 The Altar Is Rebuilt; Worship Begins Again; Rebuilding the Altar; Worship Restored at Jerusalem; Restoration of altar and temple
\p
\v 1 In the seventh¦218082 month¦218081, the Israelis¦218084 from their \add various\add* cities¦218085, gathered¦218087 together \add ≈in unity\add* in Yerushalem¦218093.
\v 2 Then¦218122 Yotsadak's¦218100 son Yeshua¦218097 and his brothers the priests¦218102, and Shealti'el's¦218106 son Zerubavel¦218103 and his brothers, and they¦218108 built the altar¦218111 to offer¦218114 up¦218114 burnt¦218116 offerings¦218116 to Yisrael's¦218113 god¦218112 on¦218118 it¦218115 as is¦218117 written¦218117 in¦218118 the law¦218118 of Mosheh¦218119, the man¦218120 of God¦218112.\x + \xo 3:2: \xt Exo 27:1.\x*
\v 3 They¦218124 set the altar¦218125 up on its¦218128 foundation¦218128 because¦218132 they were worried \add about trouble from\add* some of the \add other\add* people¦218132 groups \add ≈in¦218130 the region\add*. Then¦218124 they offered¦218134 burnt offerings to¦218139 Yahweh¦218139 on it \add as well as the regular\add* morning¦218141 and¦218124 evening¦218142 burnt offerings.\x + \xo 3:3: \xt Num 28:1-8.\x*
\v 4 Then¦218144 they¦218144 observed the Celebration in¦218153 Shelters as \add ≈per the written¦218149 instructions\add*\x + \xo 3:4: \xt Num 29:12-38.\x* with¦218153 a burnt¦218150 offering¦218150 each day as required.
\v 5 After¦218160 that \add was over\add*, they kept up the regular burnt¦218163 offerings, plus¦218165 those for the new moons¦218165 and¦218160 other times¦218168 that Yahweh required, as well as any free-will¦218173 offerings to¦218174 Yahweh.\x + \xo 3:5: \xt Num 28:11–29:39.\x*
\v 6 \add ≈Even though the temple¦218184 foundation¦218187 rebuilding hadn't started yet\add*, the people started sacrificing burnt¦218182 offerings¦218181 to Yahweh¦218183 \add ≈from the beginning¦218180 of¦218184 October\add*.
\s1 Rebuilding the temple
\rem /s1 Rebuilding the Temple; The Rebuilding of the Temple Begins; The People Rebuild the Temple
\p
\v 7 They donated cash¦218191 to the stone-workers¦218192 and carpenters¦218193, and food¦218194, drink¦218195, and oil¦218196 to the workers from Tsidon \add !(Sidon)\add* and Tsor \add !(Tyre)\add* to \add ≈float\add* cedar¦218201 \add logs along the coast\add* from Lebananon into Port¦218208 Yafo¦218208 \add !(Joppa¦218208)\add* with the permission¦218209 of Persian King¦218211 Koresh¦218210 \add !(Cyrus¦218210)\add*.
\rem /s1 Foundation Laid for the Temple
\p
\v 8 In¦218217 the second month¦218225 of second year¦218217 \add ≈since their return¦218219 to\add* Yerushalem, Shealtiel's¦218231 son Zerubavel¦218228 and Yotsadak's¦218235 son Yeshua¦218232, and the rest¦218236 of their brothers¦218237 the priests¦218239 and the Levites, and \add ≈everyone¦218241 except who'd returned\add* to Yerushalem from¦218244 captivity¦218244, began¦218227 work on¦218217 God's residence, and they¦218227 appointed¦218246 the Levites who were twenty¦218251 and over to act¦218254 as¦218254 overseers¦218254 for the work of \add rebuilding\add* Yahweh's¦218260 \add ≈temple\add*.
\v 9 \add ≈And¦218279\add* Yeshua¦218264 with his brothers and their sons, Kadmiel¦218267 and his sons, (all descendants of¦218269 Yehudah¦218271) \add ≈cooperated\add* to¦218273 act¦218273 as¦218273 overseers¦218273 for those doing the work¦218277 at the \add ≈temple\add* \add together with\add* Henadad's¦218282 sons \add ≈and grandsons\add*, and their brothers the Levites¦218285.
\p
\v 10 \add ≈When¦218287 the builders¦218288 had\add* laid the foundation¦218287 of¦218291 Yahweh's¦218292 temple¦218291, they¦218293 \add ≈got\add* the priests¦218294 \add ≈to stand there in¦218296 their robes\add* with their trumpets¦218296, and¦218287 Asaf's¦218300 descendants (who were Levites¦218297) with their cymbals¦218301, to praise¦218302 Yahweh \add ≈using the rhythms composed by\add* David¦218309, the \add former\add* Israeli¦218310 king¦218310.\x + \xo 3:10: \xt 1Ch 25:1.\x*
\v 11 Then they¦218314 sang¦218314 in response—praising¦218315 and¦218314 thanking¦218316 Yahweh¦218335: “\add ≈Yes,\add* he¦218319 is¦218319 good¦218319, because¦218336 his¦218323 loyal¦218323 commitment to¦218335 Yisrael¦218326 \add ≈will continue forever¦218322\add*.”
\p Then all¦218327 the people¦218329 shouted¦218330 a¦218331 great¦218333 shout¦218331 in praise¦218334 to Yahweh because the foundation¦218337 of¦218338 Yahweh's¦218317 \add temple\add* had been laid.\x + \xo 3:11: \xt 1Ch 16:34; 2Ch 5:13; 7:3; Psa 100:5; 106:1; 107:1; 118:1; 136:1; Jer 33:11.\x*
\v 12 Many¦218343 of the older¦218348 priests¦218344 and Levites¦218345, and \add ≈clan leaders\add* who'd seen¦218350 the first¦218354 \add ≈temple\add*, wept¦218359 loudly \add ≈when¦218355 they¦218350 witnessed\add* the founding¦218355 of this \add *one\add*, \add ≈but¦218343 others were¦218359 shouting¦218363 happily with¦218355 loud voices\add*.
\v 13 So¦218368 the people couldn't differentiate the happy sounds from the sound¦218374 of¦218376 the people weeping¦218375, because¦218377 the people were¦218379 shouting¦218379 \add ≈very loudly and¦218368 it¦218383 could be heard¦218383 from far away\add*.
\c 4
\s1 Opposition to rebuilding the temple
\rem /s1 Opposition to the Rebuilding; Opposition to the Rebuilding of the Temple; Enemies Oppose the Rebuilding; Resistance to Rebuilding the Temple
\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now\add* the enemies of Yehudah¦218391 and¦218392 Benyamin¦218392 heard¦218389 that¦218393 the \add ≈Israelis¦218400 who'd come back from\add* exile¦218396 were¦218397 building¦218397 a temple¦218398 for¦218399 Yisrael's¦218401 god¦218400 Yahweh¦218399.
\v 2 \add ≈so\add* they went to Zerubavel¦218406 and to the \add other\add* \add ≈clan leaders\add* and they said¦218411 to them¦218412, “Let¦218413 us \add ≈help you with¦218414 the building¦218413 work\add*, because¦218415 like¦218416 you, we \add ≈worship\add* your god¦218418 and we've¦218422 been sacrificing¦218423 to him since¦218424 the days¦218424 of¦218424 the Assyrian king¦218427 Esar¦218425-Haddon—the one who¦218429 \add ≈sent\add* us here.”\x + \xo 4:2: \xt 2Ki 17:24-41.\x*
\p
\v 3 \add ≈But¦218433\add* Zerubavel¦218435, and Yeshua¦218436, and the rest¦218437 of¦218438 the \add ≈Israelis¦218440 clan leaders\add* said¦218433 to them, “It's not for you¦218443 and for us to build a house¦218446 for our¦218447 god, but¦218433 we ourselves together¦218450 will¦218451 build for Yisrael's¦218440 god¦218447 Yahweh¦218452, just¦218455 as¦218455 the Persian King¦218457 Koresh \add !(Cyrus¦218458)\add* has commanded¦218456 us.”
\p
\v 4 \add ≈Those local\add* people had been discouraging the people of¦218469 Yehudah¦218471 and¦218463 trying to stop them from building¦218475.
\v 5 They'd \add also\add* hired \add ≈influencers to work against¦218478 them throughout the reigns¦218490\add* of the Persian kings¦218486 Koresh¦218485 \add !(Cyrus¦218485)\add* and¦218488 Dareyavesh¦218491 \add !(Darius¦218491)\add*.
\s1 The opposition of replacement of Yerushalem
\rem /s1 Rebuilding of Jerusalem Opposed; Later Opposition Under Xerxes and Artaxerxes; Later Opposition under King Artaxerxes; Opposition to the Rebuilding of Jerusalem
\p
\v 6 Now at¦218496 the beginning¦218498 of the reign¦218496 of Ahashverosh¦218497 \add !(Ahasuerus¦218497 or Xerxes¦218497)\add*, they¦218500 \add ≈forwarded\add* an¦218501 accusation¦218501 against those who lived in¦218496 Yerushalem¦218506 and¦218506 \add throughout\add* Yehudah¦218505.
\p
\v 7 And¦218509 in the days¦218509 of Persian King¦218522 Artahshasta \add !(Artaxerxes¦218510)\add*, Bishlam¦218512, Mitredat¦218513, Taveel and the rest¦218515 of \add #their\add* companions wrote¦218511 to¦218518 the king¦218522. (The letter¦218526 was¦218527 written¦218527 in Aramaic¦218528 \add !(Syrian¦218528)\add* and \add ≈using that alphabet\add*).
\p
\v 8 Rehum¦218533 \add ≈the high commissioner\add* and¦218537 Shimshai¦218537 the \add ≈provincial secretary\add* wrote¦218539 a letter¦218540 to¦218545 King¦218546 Artahshasta¦218545 against Yerushalem¦218544 as¦218547 follows¦218547:
\p
\v 9 \add From\add* Rehum¦218550 \add ≈the high commissioner\add* and Shimshai¦218554 the \add ≈provincial secretary\add*, and the \add ≈our\add* companions, the judges and the rulers, the officials¦218561, the Persians, the Erechites, the Babylonians, the Susaites (that is, the Elamites),
\v 10 and the rest¦218571 of the nations that¦218573 the famous and powerful \add King\add* Asenappar¦218575 exiled¦218574 \add from other nations\add* and \add ≈forced\add* them to live in¦218580 the cities¦218580 of Shomron¦218582 \add !(Samaria¦218582)\add*, and the \add ≈province went of the Euphrates river¦218586\add*.
\p And¦218587 now¦218587
\v 11 this¦218589 is¦218590 \add ≈what the letter¦218591 said\add* that¦218592 they¦218593 sent¦218593 to him¦218594:
\p To¦218597 Artahshasta¦218597 \add !(Artaxerxes¦218597)\add* the king¦218598 \add from\add* your¦218599 servants¦218599 \add ≈on this side of\add* the river¦218605.
\p And¦218598 now¦218606
\v 12 let¦218610 it¦218610 be¦218610 known¦218609 to the king¦218611 that the Jews¦218613 who¦218614 \add ≈left your region\add* have come¦218620 to us¦218619 at Yerushalem¦218621 \add ≈to\add* rebuild that rebellious¦218623 and evil¦218624 city¦218622—they're¦218627 \add currently\add* finishing¦218630 the walls¦218628 and repairing¦218633 the \add building\add* foundations¦218632.
\v 13 Now let¦218637 it¦218637 be¦218637 known¦218636 to¦218638 the king¦218638 that if¦218640 that city¦218641 is built¦218643 and the walls¦218644 are completed, \add @those people\add* won't¦218650 \add ≈pay\add* \add #taxes¦218648\add*, \add or send\add* \add #tributes¦218646\add*, and \add ≈your royal treasury will lose out\add*.
\v 14 Now¦218666, because we've \add ≈had the favour\add* of¦218662 the palace¦218663, and \add ≈because we don't¦218667 want to see¦218670 the king dishonoured¦218665\add*, \add ≈that's why we've sent¦218674 this¦218673 letter to update\add* the king,
\v 15 so that he¦218679 can search¦218679 in¦218680 the \add ≈official records¦218682 of the kingdom\add*. You'll discover¦218685 and learn¦218688 that that city \add of Yerushalem\add* is¦218692 a rebellious¦218693 city and one that has caused harm to kings¦218695 and provinces¦218696, and \add ≈has harboured rebellion¦218693 there for decades past\add*—\add ≈that's why\add* that city was¦218709 destroyed.
\v 16 We are letting the king¦218713 know¦218711 that if¦218715 that city¦218716 is \add ≈rebuilt\add* and¦218719 its walls¦218719 are completed, \add ≈then you'll lose control of this province¦218724 on¦218724 this side of the Euphrates\add*.”
\p
\v 17 The king¦218733 sent¦218732 this reply¦218731:
\p “To Rehum¦218736 \add ≈the high commissioner\add* and Shimshai¦218740 \add ≈the provincial secretary\add*, and the rest of their¦218743 companions who¦218744 live in Shomron¦218746 \add !(Samaria¦218746)\add*, and the rest of \add ≈the people in the province west of the Euphrates\add*: Peace¦218751.
\p And¦218752 now¦218752
\v 18 the¦218755 letter¦218755 that¦218756 you¦218757 all sent¦218757 to us¦218758 has been carefully read¦218760 aloud¦218760 to me¦218761.
\v 19 \add ≈I ordered my officials to search¦218766\add* \add the records\add* and discovered¦218767 \add that it's true\add* that that city¦218769 has¦218781 been \add ≈rebellious¦218779 and seditious¦218780\add* since ancient times.
\v 20 Powerful kings¦218785 have \add ≈reigned from\add* Yerushalem¦218790 and ruled¦218791 the entire¦218792 region¦218793 that side of the river¦218794, and had taxes¦218796 and tributes¦218795 paid¦218798 to¦218799 them¦218799.
\v 21 \add ≈So command those¦218807 Jews to stop rebuilding\add* the city¦218808 until¦218812 \add ≈such time as I make\add* a decree.
\v 22 \add ≈Don't be¦218819 negligent¦218820 in doing¦218821 that¦218824 or the damage¦218827 to this kingdom might get worse\add*.”
\p
\v 23 When King¦218841 Artahshasta's letter¦218837 \add reached\add* Rehum¦218845, Shimshai¦218846 the \add ≈secretary\add*, and their companions, and was read¦218842 aloud¦218842 to them all, they¦218849 \add ≈immediately\add* went¦218849 to Yerushalem¦218851 and \add ≈used force¦218857 to stop\add* the Jews \add from their rebuilding\add*.
\rem /s1 Work on the Temple Begins Again; The Rebuilding Resumes
\p
\v 24 \add ≈So there was a period when the rebuilding of the temple in Yerushalem¦218868 stopped\add*, and¦218869 it¦218862 \add ≈remained paused\add* until¦218871 the second year¦218872 of King¦218876 Dareyavesh's¦218875 reign¦218874 in Persia¦218878.\x + \xo 4:24: \xt Hag 1:1; Zech 1:1.\x*
\c 5
\s1 The temple rebuilding continues
\rem /s1 Restoration of the Temple Resumed; Tattenai's Letter to Darius
\p
\v 1 Then the prophet¦218883 Haggai¦218882 and Iddo's¦218888 son¦218886 Zekaryah¦218885 prophesied¦218881 to¦218891 the Jews in Yerushalem¦218896 and \add ≈across\add* Yehudah¦218895 in the name¦218897 of¦218898 Yisrael's¦218899 god¦218898 \add ≈who¦218900 they served\add*.\x + \xo 5:1: \xt Hag 1:1; Zech 1:1.\x*
\v 2 Then¦218903 Shealtiel's¦218908 son Zerubabel¦218905 and Yotsadak's¦218912 son Yeshua¦218909 \add ≈took action\add* and began¦218913 to¦218914 \add ≈rebuild¦218914\add* God's¦218916 \add ≈temple\add* in¦218918 Yerushalem¦218918, and the prophets¦218920 \add ≈who served\add* God were¦218919 \add there\add* with¦218918 them, supporting¦218925 them.\x + \xo 5:2: \xt Hag 1:12; Zech 4:6-9.\x*
\p
\v 3 At¦218929 that¦218951 time¦218931, Tattenai¦218934, the governor¦218935 of \add ≈the province west of the Euphrates\add*, and Shetar¦218939-Bozenai, and their¦218941 companions came¦218932 to them¦218944 and \add ≈demanded\add*, “Who¦218945 \add ≈gave you¦218948 all permission to rebuild¦218952 this¦218954 temple\add*?”
\v 4 \add ≈They¦218964 also asked the Jews to¦218961 tell them¦218961 the names¦218965 of¦218965 the men¦218966 who¦218967 were working\add* on the building.
\v 5 \add ≈However, God¦218974 was watching over the Jewish leaders\add*, and¦218973 they weren't \add actually\add* stopped. \add ≈A report¦218986 was sent¦218990\add* to¦218987 \add King\add* Dareyavesh¦218987, \add ≈then¦218973 they waited for a response\add*.
\rem /s1 Tattenai's Letter to King Darius
\v 6 Tattenai¦219002, the governor¦219004 of \add ≈the province west of the river¦219007\add*, and Shetar¦219008-Bozenai and his¦219010 companions, the \add ≈provincial\add* officials¦219011, sent¦219001 the letter¦218998 to¦219015 King¦219018 Dareyavesh \add !(Darius¦219017)\add*—
\v 7 this¦219023 is what was¦219024 written¦219024 in¦219025 their report:
\p “To¦219026 King¦219027 Dareyavesh. All¦219029 peace¦219028.
\v 8 Let¦219034 it be¦219034 known¦219032 to the king¦219035 that¦219052 we¦219038 went¦219038 to the province¦219040 of Yehudah¦219039, to the \add ≈temple\add* of the great¦219043 God¦219042, and it is being built¦219045 with¦219050 large¦219043 stones¦219046, and timber¦219048 is being placed in¦219050 the walls¦219050. This¦219052 work¦219051 is being done¦219054 \add ≈to a high standard\add* and \add ≈they're making good progress\add*.
\p
\v 9 “Then¦219059 we asked¦219060 those¦219062 elders¦219061, ‘Who¦219068 \add ≈gave you¦219071 all permission to¦219075 rebuild¦219075 this¦219077 temple\add*?’
\v 10 We also asked¦219082 them their names, so that¦219087 we¦219088 could write¦219088 down the names of \add ≈their leaders\add* to inform¦219086 you¦219086.
\p
\v 11 “This is the answer they¦219101 \add ≈gave¦219098\add* us¦219098, ‘We¦219100 are servants¦219102 of the god¦219105 of the heavens¦219106 and earth¦219107, and we¦219100 are \add ≈rebuilding¦219108 the temple\add* that¦219110 was¦219112 constructed and finished¦219122 many years¦219116 \add ≈ago by a famous Israeli¦219119\add* king¦219118.
\v 12 However, because our¦219129 ancestors¦219129 made the god¦219130 of the heavens¦219131 angry, he let Babylonian King¦219136 Nevukadnetstsar¦219135 (\add Nebuchadnezzar,\add* the Chaldean¦219139) \add ≈defeat them\add*, and he destroyed¦219143 \add ≈that¦219142 temple\add* and caused the people¦219144 to be exiled¦219145 to Babylon¦219138.\x + \xo 5:12: \xt 2Ki 25:8-12; 2Ch 36:17-20; Jer 52:12-15.\x*
\v 13 But in¦219150 the first year¦219150 \add of the reign of\add* Babylonian¦219153 King¦219153 Koresh¦219153 \add !(Cyrus¦219153)\add*, \add *he\add* made¦219158 a decree¦219159 to rebuild¦219164 this house¦219160 of God¦219162.\x + \xo 5:13: \xt Ezr 1:2-11.\x*
\v 14 \add ≈What's more,\add* the gold¦219174 and silver¦219175 \add ≈containers\add* that Nevukadnetstsar¦219177 had taken out from that temple that was¦219183 in Yerushalem¦219183 and had brought to the temple in Babylon, King¦219192 Koresh¦219191 took them out from the temple in Babylon and they¦219198 were¦219198 \add ≈handed¦219198 over\add* to the man named Sheshbatstsar¦219199 who he'd appointed¦219203 as governor¦219202 \add over Yehudah\add*.
\v 15 \add @Koresh\add* had told him to take¦219212 those¦219209 containers and put them¦219216 back in the temple in Yerushalem¦219219, and \add ≈to ensure that¦219218 the temple got rebuilt in the same place¦219225 where it¦219222 had been before\add*.
\v 16 \add ≈So\add* Sheshbatstsar¦219229 came¦219231 \add here\add* and laid¦219232 the foundation¦219233 of God's¦219237 house¦219236 in¦219239 Yerushalem¦219239, and since then¦219242, it's¦219246 been being¦219246 rebuilt but¦219240 isn't¦219247 finished¦219248 yet.’
\p
\v 17 \add ≈So¦219250\add* now¦219250, if it \add ≈pleases\add* the king, let a search¦219256 be¦219256 made¦219273 in \add the records in\add* the king's¦219261 treasure¦219258 house there¦219262 in Babylon¦219264, if it's¦219273 \add correct\add* that¦219263 a decree¦219274 was¦219273 set by King¦219254 Koresh¦219271 to rebuild¦219275 this house of¦219276 God¦219278 in Yerushalem¦219280. Then¦219250 let the king send¦219286 his decision¦219281 on¦219264 this matter back to us¦219287.”
\c 6
\s1 The former approval is found
\rem /s1 The Decree of Darius; Emperor Cyrus' Order Is Rediscovered; Darius Approves the Rebuilding
\p
\v 1 \add ≈So\add* King¦219292 Dareyavesh \add !(Darius¦219291)\add* \add ≈ordered that a search¦219295 be conducted\add* in \add all\add* the \add ≈archives¦219298\add* where¦219299 treasures¦219300 had been deposited¦219301 there¦219302 in Babylon¦219303,
\v 2 and one scroll¦219311 was¦219305 found¦219305 in the fortress at¦219306 Ecbatana¦219306 in the province¦219310 of Media¦219309, and this \add ≈record¦219317 had been made\add*:
\p
\v 3 “In¦219320 year¦219320 one¦219321 of Koresh¦219322 the king, \add *he¦219326\add* made¦219326 a decree¦219327 about¦219328 the house¦219328 of God¦219330 in¦219331 Yerushalem¦219331:
\m ‘Let the house be¦219333 built¦219333 in the \add same\add* place¦219334 where sacrifices¦219337 were¦219337 \add ≈made\add*. \add ≈Establish\add* its foundations¦219339 and \add ≈build it¦219333 27m high and 27m wide\add*
\v 4 with three¦219353 layers of large \add #stones¦219351\add* and¦219354 a layer of new¦219358 timber¦219357. \add ≈That¦219363 should¦219364 all be paid for from¦219360 the royal treasury\add*.
\v 5 Also¦219366, the gold¦219372 and silver¦219373 containers from the house of God that¦219374 Nevukadnetstsar¦219375 had taken out¦219376 from the Yerushalem temple and had brought¦219376 to Babylon¦219384, must be returned to their places¦219391 in the temple in Yerushalem. \add ≈So¦219366\add* you¦219392 must put them¦219392 in the house of God.’ ”
\s1 King Dareyavesh orders resumption of work
\rem /s1 Emperor Darius Orders the Work to Continue
\p
\v 6 \add Therefore King Dareyavesh wrote:\add* “Now¦219397 to Governor¦219399 Tattenai¦219398 \add ≈in the province west of¦219399 the Euphrates\add*, Shetar¦219403-Bozenai¦219404, and¦219405 their¦219405 companions, the officials¦219407 who¦219408 in that province:
\p \add ≈Keep away from¦219413 that place\add*.
\v 7 Leave¦219417 alone the work¦219418 on that house of God¦219421. Let the Jewish governor¦219423 and¦219425 elders¦219425 build¦219431 that \add ≈temple\add* in its¦219434 place¦219434.
\v 8 \add ≈So¦219436 here's my decree¦219438 about¦219445 what¦219439 should¦219461 be done¦219442 for\add* those Jewish elders¦219445 to¦219439 build¦219448 that house¦219449 of God¦219451: Using the king's¦219454 treasures¦219453 that come from¦219453 the tribute¦219456 of that west-Euphrates province, let¦219461 \add ≈those workers costs be regularly reimbursed\add* so that \add @the work\add* doesn't stop.
\v 9 Whatever¦219470 is needed¦219471 (\add ≈including¦219472 young\add* bulls¦219473, or rams¦219474, or lambs¦219475 for¦219477 burnt¦219477 offerings¦219477 to the god¦219479 of the heavens¦219480, wheat¦219481, salt¦219482, wine¦219484, or oil¦219485, according¦219486 to the command of the priests¦219487 in¦219490 Yerushalem¦219490), let it¦219491 be¦219491 given¦219492 to them¦219493 day by day (that¦219497 is, without delay),
\v 10 so that they¦219504 can be¦219504 offering¦219505 sweet-smelling sacrifices to¦219507 the god¦219511 of the heavens¦219508 and praying¦219509 for¦219510 the life¦219510 of the king¦219511 and his¦219512 sons¦219512.
\v 11 \add ≈Also¦219514 I\add* decree¦219516 that¦219524 any man who¦219521 changes this¦219524 edict¦219523 should have a beam¦219526 pulled¦219525 from¦219527 his house, and \add after it's sharpened and\add* \add ≈set into the ground\add*, then¦219514 he should be impaled¦219531 on¦219532 it. Then¦219514 his \add entire\add* house should be made¦219535 into a rubbish heap \add ≈because of what he did\add*.
\v 12 May¦219564 the¦219540 god¦219540 who has¦219542 established his¦219543 name¦219543 there¦219544 overthrow¦219545 any king¦219548 or person¦219549 who \add ≈makes any attempt\add* to change \add this decree or\add* to destroy¦219555 that¦219560 house¦219556 of God¦219540 in¦219561 Yerushalem¦219561. I¦219562, Dareyavesh¦219563, have \add ≈made\add* a decree¦219565. Let¦219567 it¦219567 be¦219567 done¦219567 diligently¦219566.”
\s1 The temple dedication
\rem /s1 The Temple Is Dedicated; The Temple's Dedication; Completion and Dedication of the Temple
\p
\v 13 Then¦219570 Tattenai¦219571, the governor¦219572 of \add ≈the region¦219573 west of the Euphrates\add*, Shetar¦219576-Bozenai¦219577, and¦219578 their¦219578 companions \add ≈worked hard to¦219579 follow the instructions sent¦219582 by King¦219584 Dareyavesh\add* \add !(Darius¦219583)\add*.
\v 14 \add ≈So¦219589\add* the Jewish elders¦219589 \add ≈continued\add* building¦219591, and \add ≈they were encouraged\add* by¦219593 the prophesying¦219593 of the prophet¦219595 Haggai¦219594 and Iddo's¦219600 son¦219598 Zekaryah¦219597. \add ≈As a result of the decrees of the Persian kings¦219612 Koresh¦219609, and Dareyavesh¦219610 and Artahshasta\add*, they \add ≈were able to fulfil God's¦219606 decree¦219608 to rebuild\add* \add the temple\add*.\x + \xo 6:14: a \xt Hag 1:1; \xo b \xt Zech 1:1.\x*
\v 15 The \add rebuilt\add* \add ≈temple\add* was finished¦219615 in \add ≈mid-March\add* in the sixth year¦219626 of King¦219631 Dareyavesh's¦219630 reign¦219629.
\p
\v 16 Then the \add ≈Israeli¦219637 people¦219635\add*, the priests¦219638, and the Levites¦219639, and the \add ≈ones that¦219648 had returned from\add* exile¦219643, performed the dedication¦219644 of this house¦219645 of God¦219647 with¦219649 \add ≈celebrations¦219634\add*.
\v 17 \add During\add* the dedication¦219652, they¦219651 offered¦219651 a hundred bulls¦219657, two-hundred rams¦219659, and¦219651 four-hundred lambs¦219661, as well as twelve male goats¦219665 for a sin¦219666 offering¦219666 for all¦219670 Yisrael¦219672 (matching the number¦219676 of¦219676 the tribes¦219677).
\v 18 Then¦219680 they¦219680 \add ≈organised\add* the priests¦219681 to stand in their divisions¦219682 and¦219680 the Levites¦219683 in their sections \add ≈to serve\add* the god¦219688 who \add ≈resides\add* in Yerushalem¦219690, according¦219691 to the \add ≈instructions written¦219691 by\add* Mosheh¦219693 \add !(Moses¦219693)\add*.
\s1 The Feast of ‘pass-over’ of Messenger
\rem /s1 The Passover; Celebration of Passover; The Passover Celebrated
\p
\v 19 \add ≈So the people who'd returned from exile¦219699 celebrated the ‘pass-over¦219702’ in¦219703 late April\add*.\x + \xo 6:19: \xt Exo 12:1-20.\x*
\v 20 The¦219710 priests and Levites¦219711 \add ≈all had¦219709 to be individually\add* purified¦219709, and they¦219715 slaughtered¦219715 the \add ≈lambs\add* for all the \add ≈exiles¦219720\add* and for their¦219721 brothers¦219721 the priests, and for themselves¦219723.
\v 21 \add ≈Then¦219725 all the Israelis¦219728 ate¦219725\add* \add the meal\add*—those who'd returned¦219729 from the exile¦219730 and¦219725 every¦219731 one¦219732 who'd separated¦219732 themselves from the uncleanness¦219733 of the nations¦219734 of the land¦219736 in order to search¦219738 for¦219739 Israel's¦219741 god¦219740 Yahweh¦219739.
\v 22 Then¦219743 they¦219743 happily enjoyed the Flat Bread¦219746 Celebration for seven¦219747 days¦219748, because¦219750 Yahweh¦219753 had \add ≈made¦219752 them happy\add*, and¦219754 had caused the Assyrian king¦219756 \add ≈to show favour to\add* them, to \add ≈assist their¦219761 work¦219762 rebuilding\add* the house¦219763 of God¦219766, the god¦219766 of Yisrael¦219767.
\c 7
\s1 Ezra arrives in Yerushalem
\rem /s1 Ezra's mission to Jerusalem; Ezra Arrives in Jerusalem; Ezra Comes to Jerusalem; The Coming and Work of Ezra
\p
\v 1 \add ≈Many years later\add* in¦219773 the reign¦219773 of Persian King¦219775 Artahshasta \add !(Artaxerxes¦219774)\add*, Ezra¦219778 (son of Serayah¦219781, son of Azaryah¦219784, son of Hilkiyah¦219787,
\v 2 son of Shallum¦219791, son of Tsadok¦219794, son of Ahitub¦219797,
\v 3 son of Amaryah¦219801, son of Azaryah¦219804, son of Merayot¦219807,
\v 4 son of Zerahiah¦219811, son of Uzzi¦219814, son of Bukki¦219817,
\v 5 son of Avishua¦219821, the son of Pinhas¦219824, the son of Eleazar¦219827, the son of Aharon¦219830 the head¦219832 priest¦219831)
\v 6 was¦219840 a skilled¦219841 \add ≈expert\add* in¦219842 the law¦219842 that¦219844 Yisrael's¦219849 god¦219848 Yahweh had given¦219846 through Mosheh¦219843 \add !(Moses¦219843)\add*. \add ≈With¦219843 the favour of his god Yahweh helping\add* \add @Ezra¦219835\add*, the king¦219853 had granted¦219850 all¦219859 his requests¦219860, and he travelled from Babylon¦219837 \add @to Yerushalem\add*.
\v 7 \add ≈Some Israelis¦219866, including¦219863\add* some priests¦219869 and Levites¦219870, singers¦219871 and gatekeepers¦219872, and some temple¦219873 servants¦219873 \add ≈travelled\add* to¦219874 Yerushalem¦219876 in¦219877 the seventh¦219879 year¦219877 of¦219880 Artahshasta's \add ≈reign\add*.
\v 8-9 They left Babylon on New Year's¦219888 Day (in early April) and¦219883 \add ≈with¦219885 God's favour\add* \add on the journey\add*, arrived in Yerushalem¦219884 exactly four months¦219885 later
\v 10 because¦219913 Ezra¦219914 had¦219915 made \add ≈a firm resolution\add* to \add ≈study¦219917\add* Yahweh's¦219921 \add written\add* \add ≈instructions\add*, and to \add carefully\add* \add ≈follow\add* \add #them\add*, and to teach¦219923 \add *them\add* in¦219924 Yisrael¦219924.
\s1 King Artahshasta's letter to Ezra
\rem /s1 King Artaxerxes' Letter to Ezra; Artaxerxes' Letter to Ezra; The Letter of Artaxerxes to Ezra; The Document Which Emperor Artaxerxes Gave to Ezra
\p
\v 11 King¦219935 Artahshasta¦219948 \add !(Artaxerxes¦219936)\add* had given¦219934 a letter¦219932 for Ezra¦219937 the priest¦219938 and scribe and \add ≈expert\add* in Yahweh's¦219944 commands¦219942 and instructions¦219945 \add to take with him\add*, \add ≈saying\add*:
\p
\v 12 Artahshasta, the king¦219952 of kings¦219953, to¦219954 the priest¦219955 Ezra¦219954, the scribe¦219956 of the law¦219957 of the god¦219960 of heavens¦219961: Peace.
\p Now¦219963,
\v 13 \add ≈I hereby\add* decree¦219967 that¦219968 anyone¦219971 in¦219972 my¦219972 kingdom¦219972 from¦219973 Yisrael¦219976 (including¦219977 priests¦219977 and Levites¦219978) who freely offers to go to Yerushalem¦219980 with¦219972 you¦219981, may go.
\v 14 \add ≈You¦219991 are sent¦219994 by\add* the king¦219991 and his¦219993 seven¦219992 counsellors¦219993 to¦219995 \add ≈determine whether\add* \add the people of\add* Yehudah¦219998 and Yerushalem¦219999 \add ≈are following\add* the law¦220000 of your¦220001 god¦220001 which¦220002 \add ≈you¦219994 have a copy of\add*.
\v 15 \add ≡You¦220010 are also\add* to take the gold¦220007 and silver¦220006 that¦220008 the king¦220010 and his¦220017 counsellors¦220011 have¦220012 freely¦220012 offered¦220012 to the god¦220013 of¦220014 Yisrael¦220014 \add ≈who¦220015 lives\add* in¦220016 Jerusalem¦220016,
\v 16 along with all the gold¦220021 and silver¦220020 that¦220022 you¦220023 \add ≈collect\add* all \add ≈across\add* Babylon¦220026, along with the freewill¦220028 \add #offerings¦220028\add* of the people¦220029 and the priests¦220030 who¦220031 freely¦220031 give towards the house¦220032 of God¦220033 in¦220024 Yerushalem¦220035.
\p
\v 17 \add ≈So then\add* you should diligently¦220041 \add ≈use those funds\add* to buy¦220042 bulls¦220045, rams¦220047, lambs¦220048, and \add supplies for\add* their¦220049 grain¦220049 offerings and drink¦220050 offerings, and you should offer¦220051 them¦220052 on¦220043 the altar¦220055 at¦220043 the your god's¦220058 house¦220057 in¦220043 Yerushalem¦220060.
\v 18 With \add ≈the remaining funds\add*, you can \add ≈use them for\add* whatever¦220062 seems good¦220072 to you and¦220062 your brothers¦220069, according¦220077 to the will¦220077 of¦220077 your god¦220078.
\v 19 \add ≈Also¦220081, make¦220089 sure that\add* you deliver all those \add gold and silver\add* containers that were \add ≈handed¦220084 over\add* to¦220085 you for use in your¦220088 god's house¦220087 in Yerushalem¦220092.
\v 20 \add ≈Anything¦220108 else that's\add* needed¦220095 for the house¦220096 of¦220096 your¦220097 god¦220097 that \add ≈you¦220103 need to supply can be provided¦220102\add* from¦220104 the king's¦220108 treasuries¦220107.
\p
\v 21 And I¦220111, King¦220113 Artahshasta \add ≈make¦220114\add* a decree¦220115 for all the treasurers¦220117 \add ≈in¦220119 the province¦220119 west of\add* the river¦220120: that you all diligently¦220134 help with¦220119 everything that the priest¦220127 Ezra¦220126 (the scribe¦220128 of the law¦220129 of the god¦220132 of the heavens¦220133) asks¦220125 from you all—
\v 22 up to¦220137 three tonnes of silver¦220139, five hundred bushels of wheat¦220144, two thousand litres of wine¦220149 and \add ≈the same amount\add* of olive oil¦220155, and \add ≈as much salt¦220157 as he needs\add*.
\v 23 Everything¦220184 that¦220165 the god¦220169 of the heavens¦220170 decreed¦220168 to be done should¦220171 be done exactly¦220172 \add ≈as he specified because there's no good reason to make him angry at\add* the kingdom¦220183 of the king¦220184 and¦220185 his¦220185 sons¦220185?
\v 24 \add ≈Also¦220187, it should be made¦220188 clear\add* that there is no authority¦220205 to \add ≈extract\add* \add #taxes¦220202\add* or tribute¦220201 from any priests¦220192 or Levites¦220193, singers¦220194 or the gatekeepers¦220195, the temple¦220196 servants or the servants of that house¦220198 of God¦220199.
\p
\v 25 As for you, Ezra¦220210, \add ≈use the wisdom¦220211 that your god has given to you to\add* appoint¦220216 magistrates and¦220209 judges¦220217 who can judge¦220218 all¦220224 the people¦220226 who are in¦220215 \add that province\add* beyond¦220228 the river¦220229—everyone¦220226 who know the laws¦220233 of your god (plus¦220218 you should teach those¦220232 who don't¦220236 know \add >them\add*).
\v 26 Anyone¦220253 who¦220242 \add ≈refuses to obey\add* your¦220250 god's¦220250 laws and¦220240 the king's¦220253 laws, \add ≈should¦220256 receive swift\add* judgement¦220255—whether¦220259 it's confiscation¦220266 of goods, or banishment¦220262, imprisonment¦220268, or \add ≈the death¦220260 sentence\add*.”
\s1 Ezra praises Yahweh
