\p
\v 15 \add Firstly,\add* I gathered¦220479 them¦220479 \add ≈near\add* the river¦220482 that goes¦220483 to¦220484 Ahava¦220486, and we camped¦220487 there¦220488 for three¦220490 days¦220489. I \add ≈interviewed\add* the people¦220492 and the priests¦220493 and \add ≈discovered that we didn't¦220496 have any Levites included\add* \add in the group\add*.
\v 16 \add ≈So¦220501 I summoned\add* the following leaders¦220511: Eliezer¦220502, Ariel¦220503, Shemayah¦220504, Elnatan, Yarib¦220506, \add a second\add* Elnatan, Natan¦220508, Zekaryah¦220509, and Meshullam¦220510, as well as the wise men: Yoyariv¦220512 and \add a third\add* Elnatan.
\v 17 I commanded¦220516 them to go to Iddo, the leader¦220522 at¦220523 Kasifya, and I \add ≈told¦220516 them to tell\add* Iddo and his¦220532 relatives (temple servants¦220540 in Kasifya) to send us \add @some Levites\add* who would \add go to Yerushalem to\add* serve in our god's¦220542 \add ≈temple\add*.
\v 18 \add ≈Then¦220544 since¦220546 we had God's¦220561 favour\add*, they¦220544 sent us a \add ≈talented\add* man¦220551 (from¦220553 the¦220553 sons of Mahli¦220554, son of Levi¦220557, son of Yisrael¦220560) and eighteen¦220564 of his¦220563 sons and \add ≈other relatives\add*.
\v 19 \add They also sent\add* Hashavyah¦220569 and Yeshayah¦220571 (from¦220572 Merari's¦220573 sons), and their¦220575 relatives and sons—some twenty¦220576 men—
\v 20 plus¦220579 two¦220588 hundred¦220588 and twenty¦220589 \add descendants of\add* Levite¦220586 temple¦220587 servants¦220587 that \add King\add* David¦220583 and his officials¦220584 had¦220591 appointed¦220582 for service—all designated¦220591 by¦220592 name¦220592.
\s1 Ezra's fasting and praying
\rem /s1 Fasting and Prayer for Protection; Ezra Leads the People in Fasting and Prayer
\p
\v 21 Then¦220594 \add right\add* there¦220595 by the river¦220599 Ahava¦220600, I proclaimed¦220594 a fast¦220596 to humble¦220601 ourselves¦220601 \add ≈in¦220602 front¦220602 of\add* our god¦220603 to \add ≈request¦220604 that he'd smooth the\add* way \add ahead\add* for us¦220608, and for our children¦220609, and for all¦220610 our property¦220612,
\v 22 because¦220625 I¦220615 was¦220615 ashamed¦220615 to request¦220637 an army and horsemen¦220621 from the king to help¦220622 us¦220622 from \add ≈possible enemies¦220623\add* on¦220624 the way. \add ≈Also, you see,\add* we¦220627 had¦220627 \add previously\add* told the king, “Our god¦220632 \add ≈does\add* good¦220638 to all those who \add ≈honour\add* him, but¦220621 his might and his \add ≈anger¦220640\add* are¦220641 against all those who abandon¦220644 him.”
\v 23 \add ≈So¦220646\add* we¦220646 fasted¦220646 and sought¦220647 \add wisdom\add* from¦220648 our god¦220648 concerning this¦220651, and he¦220652 \add ≈listened¦220652 to¦220653 our requests\add*.
\s1 The gift and donations for the temple
\rem /s1 Gifts for the Temple; The Gifts for the Temple
\p
\v 24 Then¦220655 I chose twelve of the leaders¦220656 of the priests¦220657 along¦220660 with Sherevyah and Hashavyah¦220661 and ten¦220664 of the other Levites,
\v 25 and \add as they watched,\add* I weighed¦220666 out¦220666 the gold¦220675 and silver¦220672, and the \add valuable\add* utensils—the offering for the house¦220680 of our¦220682 god¦220682 that¦220683 the king¦220684, and his¦220685 counsellors¦220685 and officials¦220686, and all¦220687 the \add ≈exiled Israelis¦220689 who¦220690 could be contacted\add*, had¦220683 offered¦220683.
\v 26 \add ≈It came to\add* three tonnes of gold¦220707, twenty-one tonnes of silver, and¦220692 another three tonnes of silver containers,
\v 27 as well as twenty¦220713 gold bowls¦220711 that weighed another eight kilograms, and¦220711 two¦220720 polished bronze¦220717 containers that were as valuable as gold.
\p
\v 28 “You are sacred to Yahweh,” I told them all, “and the \add ≈containers and utensils\add* are sacred, and the gold¦220732 and silver¦220731 are a freewill¦220733 offering¦220733 to Yahweh, the god¦220735 of your¦220736 ancestors¦220736.
\v 29 \add ≈Look after them all carefully\add* until¦220740 you weigh¦220742 them out¦220742 \add ≈in front¦220743\add* of the leaders of the priests¦220745 and Levites¦220746 and the leaders of the Israeli¦220750 elders in the chambers¦220752 of Yahweh's¦220754 house¦220753 in Yerushalem¦220751.”
\v 30 So¦220756 the priests¦220757 and the Levites¦220758 \add ≈accepted\add* the \add ≈receipt\add* of the gold¦220761 and silver¦220760, and the containers, to take¦220756 them to Yerushalem¦220764—to the house¦220765 of our¦220766 god¦220766.
\s1 The return to Yerushalem
\rem /s1 The Return to Jerusalem
\p
\v 31 Then in¦220772 mid-April, we set¦220769 out¦220769 from the river¦220770 Ahava¦220771 to go¦220776 to Yerushalem¦220777, and \add ≈we had God's¦220780 favour as he¦220783 kept us¦220783 safe from any enemies¦220785 or ambushes¦220786\add* on¦220772 the way¦220789.
\v 32 \add ≈So¦220791\add* we arrived at Yerushalem¦220792, and¦220793 \add ≈rested\add* there¦220794 for three¦220796 days¦220795.
\v 33 On¦220798 the fourth¦220799 day¦220798, the gold¦220802 and silver¦220801 and the \add ≈containers and utensils\add* were weighed¦220800 out in¦220798 the \add ≈temple\add*—\add ≈being handed over to\add* Uriyah's¦220812 son Meremot¦220809, the priest¦220813, and with him¦220814 was Pinhas's¦220818 son Eleazar¦220815 (and with them¦220819 were Yeshua's¦220823 son Yozavad¦220820, and Binnuy's¦220827 son Noadyah¦220824, the Levites¦220828).
\v 34 \add ≈They recorded¦220833 all¦220834 the¦220836 items with¦220831 their weights¦220836\add*.
\p
\v 35 The \add ≈descendants of the former captives¦220842 who had returned from\add* exile¦220845 offered burnt offerings¦220847 to Yisrael's¦220850 god¦220849: twelve bulls¦220851 for all¦220857 Yisrael, 96 rams¦220860, 77 lambs¦220864, then twelve male goats for a sin¦220868 offering. The whole¦220857 was¦220872 \add presented as\add* a burnt offering to Yahweh¦220873.
\v 36 They¦220876 \add ≈relayed\add* the king's¦220881 orders to¦220882 the governors¦220884 and officials of \add the province\add* beyond the river¦220886, and so they¦220887 honoured the people¦220890 and God's¦220895 house¦220893.
\c 9
\s1 Ezra's reaction against mixed marriages
\rem /s1 Measures against mixed marriages; Denunciation of Mixed Marriages; Ezra's Prayer About Intermarriage; Ezra Learns of Intermarriages with Non-Jews; Ezra's Prayer concerning Intermarriage
\p
\v 1 Now as soon as those¦220899 things were finished¦220898, the leaders¦220902 came to me, saying¦220903, “The people¦220907 of Yisrael¦220908, and the priests¦220909 and Levites¦220910 haven't kept themselves¦220906 separate¦220906 from¦220911 \add ≈the idolatry of\add* the peoples¦220911 of the lands¦220912: the \add #Canaanites¦220914, Hittites¦220915, Perizzites¦220916, the Yebusites¦220917, Ammonites¦220918, Moabites, Egyptians, and the Amorites¦220921\add*.
\v 2 \add ≈Instead\add*, they've \add ≈taken¦220925 women¦220926 from those peoples as wives\add* for¦220927 themselves¦220929 and their sons¦220928, so they've \add ≈diluted their sacred¦220931 heritage with¦220932 the anti-God customs of those peoples\add*. \add ≈But¦220928 the worst is that\add* it's \add &our\add* leaders¦220935 and officials¦220936 that have been¦220937 at¦220932 the forefront in¦220932 this¦220939 unfaithfulness¦220938.”
\v 3 As soon as I heard¦220943 that¦220947, I tore¦220948 my \add ≈clothes\add* and pulled¦220953 some of the hair¦220954 out of my head¦220955 and beard¦220956, and I sat¦220957 down¦220957 appalled¦220958.
\v 4 \add ≈Any others who respectfully followed Yisrael's¦220967 god's¦220965 instructions\add* \add and who were concerned\add* \add ≈about¦220964 the unfaithfulness¦220969 of the exiles¦220970, joined with¦220964 me\add* and I¦220971 sat¦220972 there appalled¦220973 until¦220974 \add the time of\add* the evening¦220976 sacrifice.
\s1 Ezra's prayer
\rem /s1 Ezra's Prayer
\p
\v 5 \add ≈So¦220978\add* I got up from¦220981 my \add position of\add* humilation¦220981 with¦220978 my torn¦220982 \add ≈clothes\add* \add during\add* the evening¦220979 sacrifice, then¦220978 I \add ≈went\add* down¦220985 on¦220978 my knees¦220988 and¦220978 spread¦220989 out¦220989 my palms¦220990 to¦220991 my god¦220994 Yahweh¦220993
\v 6 and \add ≈prayed\add*, “My god¦220997, I'm¦220998 ashamed¦220998 and humiliated¦220998 to raise my face¦221002 to you¦221003, my god, because¦221004 our sins have¦221006 multiplied \add and risen\add* above \add ≈our heads¦221008\add*, and our guilt¦221009 has \add ≈mounted\add* up as \add ≈high as the sky\add*.
\v 7 From \add back in\add* the time¦221014 of our ancestors¦221015 until¦221019 today, \add ≈we've¦221016 been very guilty¦221017\add*, and in our \add ≈disobedience\add*, we ourselves, \add including\add* our kings and our priests¦221026, have been \add ≈killed by the kings of the surrounding countries, or taken captive¦221032, or been plundered¦221033, or simply put to shame¦221034, which is the case right now\add*.
\v 8 \add ≈But¦221039\add* now¦221039 for a brief¦221040 moment¦221042, favour¦221044 has come¦221043 from our god Yahweh¦221047 \add and given\add* us remaining survivors a stake in¦221056 his holy place¦221056—\add yes,\add* our god \add ≈has cheered us up and given us a little¦221063 relief from\add* our slavery.
\v 9 Because¦221066 we¦221069 are¦221068 slaves¦221068, yet our god hasn't abandoned¦221075 us in our slavery, but¦221070 he's¦221077 \add ≈used his loyal¦221080 commitment\add* \add to us\add* \add ≈to influence\add* the Persian¦221083 king¦221082 to give to us \add ≈breathing space\add* to \add ≈rebuild\add* the house¦221091 of our god \add ≈from\add* its¦221096 ruins¦221096, and to give to us a ‘wall¦221100 \add of protection\add*’ in Yerushalem¦221102 and \add ≈across\add* Yehudah¦221101.
\p
\v 10 “\add ≈So\add* now¦221105, our god¦221109, what can we say¦221108 after¦221110 that¦221112? We've abandoned¦221114 your¦221115 instructions
\v 11 which¦221117 you \add ≈gave us via\add* your¦221120 servants¦221120, the prophets¦221121, saying¦221122, ‘The land that you're all entering to occupy is¦221128 a land of impurity, due to the impurity of the \add ≈current inhabitants with\add* their \add ≈evil practices\add* that have¦221136 filled¦221136 it¦221136 from¦221137 \add ≈one end¦221137 to the other\add* with their \add ≈filth\add*.
\v 12 \add ≈So¦221143\add* now¦221143, don't give¦221147 your daughters¦221144 to their sons¦221153 \add to marry\add*, or \add ≈vice versa\add*. And don't \add ≈try to make long-term peace¦221157 treaties or contracts with them\add*. \add ≈Then¦221143\add* you all will \add ≈stay in power\add*, and eat¦221164 the good¦221167 things¦221167 of¦221167 the land¦221168, and \add ≈be able to pass it on to your children for all their future generations\add*.’\x + \xo 9:12: \xt Exo 34:11-16; Deu 7:1-5.\x*
\p
\v 13 “Yet¦221187 after¦221175 everything¦221176 that's \add ≈happened to us as a result\add* our evil¦221181 actions and our great¦221183 guilt¦221182 (even though you, our god¦221187, \add ≈didn't punish us as harshly as you could have¦221188\add*, and you've¦221188 \add ≈allowed us to survive as we're here now\add*),
\v 14 should we¦221196 return¦221196 to \add ≈disobeying your¦221198 instructions\add* and¦221199 to intermarrying¦221199 with those¦221202 people¦221200 groups \add ≈with their evil practices\add*? You'd \add rightfully\add* be¦221204 angry¦221204 \add enough\add* with us as \add ≈to wipe us out completely without leaving any\add* remnant¦221211 or survivors¦221212?
\v 15 Yahweh¦221215, the¦221216 god¦221216 of Yisrael¦221217, you \add ≈always do what is right¦221218\add*, because \add here\add* we are as¦221224 survivors even to this¦221225 day¦221224. \add ≈So, yes, here we are standing in front of you\add* in our¦221228 guilt¦221228, because none \add ≈of us are innocent enough to stand¦221231 in front of you because of what we've done\add*.”
\c 10
\s1 The people's acceptance of their sin
\rem /s1 The Plan for Ending Mixed Marriages; The People's Confession of Sin; The People Confess Their Sin; The People's Response
\p
\v 1 When¦221247 Ezra¦221239 prayed¦221238 and confessed¦221240 \add like that\add*, weeping¦221243 and \add ≈bowing down low in front¦221245\add* of the¦221246 \add ≈temple\add*, an extremely \add ≈large¦221252 number of Israeli¦221250\add* men¦221255 and women¦221256 and children¦221257 gathered¦221248 around him \add ≈to join in and weep aloud\add*.
\v 2 Then Yehiel's¦221271 son¦221269 Shekanyah¦221268 (from the sons¦221272 of¦221273 Eylam¦221273) answered¦221267 and \add ≈admitted\add* to¦221276 Ezra¦221276, “We ourselves have behaved unfaithfully¦221278 towards our¦221279 god¦221279 and have married¦221280 foreign¦221282 women¦221281 from the \add other\add* people¦221283 groups in¦221279 \add ≈this region\add*. \add ≈But¦221267\add* there's¦221286 still hope¦221288 for¦221289 Yisrael¦221289 concerning this.
\v 3 \add ≈So¦221294\add* now¦221294, let's¦221295 \add ≈make¦221295 an agreement¦221297\add* with our¦221298 god¦221298 to \add ≈send¦221299 all¦221300 those¦221303 women back, along with their children¦221303\add*, \add ≈following the advice\add* of¦221305 my¦221306 master¦221306 and the ones who \add ≈strive to obey God's¦221309 instructions\add*, and as per the law¦221310.
\v 4 \add ≈So take action because¦221314 this is¦221316 now in your¦221316 hands, but¦221318\add* we're with¦221319 you¦221319. \add ≈Lead strongly¦221320 and¦221321 make a clear decision\add*.”
\p
\v 5 \add ≈So\add* Ezra¦221325 \add ≈took¦221338 action\add* and made¦221326 the leaders¦221329 of¦221329 the priests¦221330 and Levites¦221331, and all¦221332 Yisrael¦221334, to \add ≈promise to implement this¦221337 decision, and they¦221338 did¦221335 so\add*.
\rem /s1 Foreign Wives and Their Children Rejected
\v 6 Then¦221340 Ezra¦221341 \add ≈left that place there¦221354 in front¦221342 of the temple\add*, and he¦221345 went to Yehohanan's¦221349 room¦221348 (Elyashiv's¦221352 son¦221350) and went in. He¦221344 didn't¦221356 eat¦221358 or drink¦221362, but¦221340 \add ≈continued\add* mourning¦221364 because¦221363 of the unfaithfulness¦221367 of the exiles¦221368.
\p
\v 7 Then \add @the leaders\add* \add ≈sent an official written notice¦221372\add* throughout Yerushalem and all Yehudah¦221373 to \add ≈all those Jews who'd returned from captivity\add*, that \add @their men\add* should assemble¦221378 in¦221373 Yerushalem.
\v 8 \add They were told that\add* it¦221391 was the decision¦221388 of the leaders¦221389 and elders¦221390 that anyone who didn't¦221383 arrive within¦221386 three¦221386 days¦221387 would then¦221381 forfeit¦221391 all¦221392 their property¦221394 and would \add ≈no longer be¦221396 considered as an Israeli\add*.
\v 9 So on¦221415 the third day¦221415 (in mid-December), all the men of Yehudah¦221406 and Benyamin¦221407 gathered in Yerushalem¦221409, and all the people¦221420 sat in the \add ≈courtyard in front of the temple\add*. They were shivering because of the rain¦221428, and \add ≈because of\add* \add the seriousness\add* of the matter¦221427.
\p
\v 10 Then the priest¦221433 Ezra¦221432 stood up and \add ≈announced\add*, “You yourselves have acted¦221437 unfaithfully¦221437 and have married¦221438 foreign¦221440 women¦221439, thus adding¦221441 to Yisrael's¦221445 guilt¦221444 \add in God's eyes\add*.
\v 11 Now¦221447 \add ≈however\add*, praise¦221449 Yahweh¦221450, the god¦221451 of your¦221453 ancestors¦221453, and do¦221454 \add ≈what he's commanded us\add* and separate¦221456 yourselves¦221456 from¦221457 \add the other religions of\add* the peoples¦221457 in this \add ≈region\add*, including¦221454 \add ≈not marrying their\add* women¦221461.”
\p
\v 12 Then¦221464 all¦221465 the¦221467 \add ≈gathered Israelis\add* answered¦221464, “\add ≈Yes, we do need to¦221472 do what you've said¦221468\add*.
\v 13 However, \add ≈it's the rainy season¦221480 now, and there's¦221482 so many people¦221478 who can't¦221487 stand¦221484 outside¦221485 for several days¦221492 while we try to¦221496 work all this¦221498 out, because¦221493 we've¦221495 done so much wrong\add*.
\v 14 \add ≈So let's¦221500 delegate our leaders¦221503 to make the decisions for all¦221507 of¦221510 us. Then we can arrange to meet together by city¦221520 with¦221510 our elders¦221518 and judges¦221522 to apply the decisions about our foreign¦221513 wives, until¦221530 God's¦221528 anger¦221526 towards us about these matters¦221531 cools down\add*.
\v 15 The only¦221535 ones who were against this \add plan\add* were Asahel's¦221539 on Yonatan¦221536 and Tikvah's¦221543 son Yahzeyah¦221540, with the support¦221551 of¦221541 Meshullam¦221548 and the Levite¦221550 Shabetai¦221549.
\p
\v 16 So¦221553 the \add ≈exiled¦221557 Israelis agreed to follow that plan\add*, and the names¦221567 \add ≈of¦221562 the men¦221561 were written down by each¦221566 clan leader who then¦221553 stayed behind with¦221567\add* the priest¦221560 Ezra¦221559, and \add ≈a few days¦221569 later,\add* they¦221568 sat down to \add ≈start working through the lists\add*.
